  "summary": "Malicious code in tinkoff-pwa-confac-types (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package downloads a platform-specific binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GETs to /pkg/package (or platform variants). It writes the binary to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (Linux/macOS) or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe (Windows) and executes it as a detached background process. A DNS TXT-record-based fallback channel at c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site (and platform-specific subdomains) provides an alternative payload delivery path. The package has no lifecycle hooks; the payload runs on module import via index.js requiring _adapter.js.",
